<Ui::Modal @title={{this.title}} @size="xl" @onClose={{@onClose}} data-test-admission-editor>
  <div class="row g-3">
    <div class="col-lg-8">
      <p class="text-secondary">
        The policy in the JSON form of the API. A rule is violated when its CEL expression does not evaluate to true;
        with the warn action the write goes through with a warning. The server compiles the expressions when the
        policy is saved and reports the errors here.
      </p>
      <Ui::Editor
        @label="Admission policy"
        @language="json"
        @schema={{this.schema}}
        @value={{this.text}}
        @onChange={{this.setText}}
        @original={{this.original}}
        @validate={{this.validate}}
        @onSubmit={{this.submit}}
        @submitLabel={{if this.isNew "Create policy" "Save policy"}}
        @permission="write admission policies"
        @onCancel={{@onClose}}
        @minHeight="20rem"
        @autofocus={{true}}
      />
    </div>
    <div class="col-lg-4">
      <Ui::Card @title="CEL reference" @size="sm" data-test-cel-reference>
        <dl class="mb-3">
          {{#each this.reference as |entry|}}
            <dt class="font-monospace">{{entry.name}}</dt>
            <dd class="small text-secondary">{{entry.text}}</dd>
          {{/each}}
        </dl>
        <div class="small fw-medium mb-1">Examples</div>
        {{#each this.examples as |example|}}
          <Ui::CodeBlock @label={{example.label}} @code={{example.code}} @wrap={{true}} @copy={{true}} class="mb-2" />
        {{/each}}
        <p class="small text-secondary mb-0">
          Use has() before optional fields: a rule that fails to evaluate counts as violated.
          Trying a policy on the existing jobs needs a dry-run endpoint the server does not have; start with warn.
        </p>
      </Ui::Card>
    </div>
  </div>
</Ui::Modal>
